rs","content":"**Concepts / vocabulary:** Concepts (Hermes, two-bot model, three-cron system, LLM gateway, Linear integration)."},"242":{"id":"/docs/architecture-161","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Operating rules / read-order:** CLAUDE.md (local), Vault/CLAUDE.md (local)."},"243":{"id":"/docs/architecture-162","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Cron inventory + Mac↔VPS parity:** Vault Rhythm."},"244":{"id":"/docs/architecture-163","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Operator cheat-sheet:** Cheat Sheet."},"245":{"id":"/docs/architecture-164","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Per-project architecture:** each project has `ARCHITECTURE.md` (Jackie-OS root, `~/dev/{newfin,rodyna,bunit,draw}/`) — read before working in that project."},"246":{"id":"/docs/architecture-165","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**B-Unit linear workflow & autonomous agents:** B-Unit repo `docs/linear-workflow.md` (agent-team dispatch)"},"247":{"id":"/docs/architecture-166","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Draw:** Draw repo `ARCHITECTURE.md`"},"248":{"id":"/docs/architecture-167","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Visual version (human-facing):** docs site \"The system map\" page."},"249":{"id":"/docs/catalog","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"page","content":"System Catalog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Look it up"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog"},"250":{"id":"/docs/catalog-0","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog","content":"Every skill and script in Jackie-OS — the map to navigate the system."},"251":{"id":"/docs/catalog-1","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"Skills vs Scripts — decision"},"252":{"id":"/docs/catalog-2","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"How it fits together (30-second orientation)"},"253":{"id":"/docs/catalog-3","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Skills — grouped by job"},"254":{"id":"/docs/catalog-4","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#what-runs-when-cron","content":"What runs when (cron)"},"255":{"id":"/docs/catalog-5","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog","content":"> **The map.** Every skill (what the AI does) and script (what runs on a schedule or on demand). Start here to navigate the system. Depth links: skills → Skills Registry; what-runs-when → Hermes VPS crontab + Vault Rhythm; operating → Cheat Sheet."},"256":{"id":"/docs/catalog-6","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Skills** are LLM judgment playbooks — markdown decision trees that agents follow when running a task (example: `morning-brief.md` = what a brief contains, how to read vault/email, when to alert, how to publish). Skills are the AI's **thinking layer**; they live in `System/skills/` and the agent reads them whole, then improvises per context."},"257":{"id":"/docs/catalog-7","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Scripts** are the mechanics layer — bash or Python executables that handle scheduling, filesystem operations, subprocess calls, and state management (example: `morning-brief-vps.py` = pull vault, run the skill in the Hermes sandbox, format output, write to file, deliver). Scripts live in `System/{coo,capture,ops,periodic,work,lib,scripts}/` and are the **source of truth** — edits go here, never the VPS copy (symlinked)."},"258":{"id":"/docs/catalog-8","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Pattern:** Skills call scripts (or describe the sequence scripts follow). A typical cron job is a thin `&#60;name>.sh` wrapper (cron entry) that execs a `&#60;name>.py` (logic). When the LLM is involved, it's one `hermes -z` call returning text that the script writes."},"259":{"id":"/docs/catalog-9","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Skills** = markdown playbooks the AI (Claude/Hermes) follows. Some are agent-run (judgment), some are implemented mechanically by a script."},"260":{"id":"/docs/catalog-10","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Scripts** = the executable layer. They live in the repo under `System/{coo,capture,ops,periodic,work,lib,scripts}/` and are the **source of truth**. On the VPS they're symlinked into `~/.hermes/scripts/` by `hermes-vps-link-scripts.sh` (rebuilt on every autodeploy `git pull`). &#x2A;*Edit the repo copy, never the VPS copy.**"},"261":{"id":"/docs/catalog-11","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Two schedulers:** the **Hermes agent-cron** (`~/.hermes/cron/jobs.json`, edited via the dashboard — the morning stack) and the **OS crontab** (`hermes-vps-crontab.txt` — deploy/health/weekly)."},"262":{"id":"/docs/catalog-12","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Pattern:** most cron jobs are a thin `&#60;name>.sh` wrapper (cron entry) that execs a `&#60;name>.py` (the logic). `no_agent` jobs are mechanical; the