able workflow playbook (markdown + optional code) living in `System/skills/`; an AI reads it and executes the defined steps. Global owned skills carry the `jos-` prefix (see Skills Registry)."},"479":{"id":"/docs/concepts-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**Hermes** — The always-on VPS agent that runs the scheduled tasks and sync loop while your Mac is off."},"480":{"id":"/docs/concepts-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**Persik** — Two Telegram bots: `@Persik_finbot` (the Newfin-hosted product bot) and `@persik_hermes_bot` (the full Hermes VPS channel)."},"481":{"id":"/docs/concepts-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**workers** — Autonomous agents building from Linear, all on the Hermes VPS as separate Cyrus instances (2026-07-23): **Fablio** (CEO/orchestrator, Fable 5 — `Plan`/`Scope` labels trigger PM modes, decomposes + delegates), **Cursorio** (fast implementer, Cursor), **Codexio** (design lead, Codex GPT-5.6 Sol + design skill pack), **Cyrusio** (delivery engineer, Sonnet 5; ex \"Cyrus Builder\"). Route work by repo label + optional mode label + assignee. Team-member rails (2026-07-23): per-agent persistent memory + shared team log in `System/agents/` (synced by the `agent-memory-sync` cron), per-agent git author identity, Telegram rail to Sergei for all four. Legacy **Codex** (ChatGPT in GitHub CI) still exists. See Linear integration below."},"482":{"id":"/docs/concepts-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**registry** — The `System/project-registry.md` file that maps each project to its code repo and/or STATUS file, serving as the single source of truth for sync."},"483":{"id":"/docs/concepts-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#occasional","content":"**janitor** — An OKF linter and maintenance tool that audits frontmatter compliance and keeps the vault structure clean (quarterly cron)."},"484":{"id":"/docs/concepts-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#occasional","content":"**docs-first** — Before building anything new, check the master index for prior art; on ship, update the owning doc in the same commit."},"485":{"id":"/docs/concepts-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#deprecated--winding-down","content":"**Cowork** — The Claude desktop app's scheduled-tasks harness on Sergei's Mac. **Effectively retired** — a single leftover schedule remains (Sunday 18:00 weekly-review); everything else runs on the VPS."},"486":{"id":"/docs/concepts-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#deprecated--winding-down","content":"**Bases/Ops board** — Obsidian Bases kanban for task tracking. **Being replaced by Linear** (migration in progress: B-Unit, Newfin, Rodyna already on Linear; Jackie-OS itself deliberately stays on Bases/markdown)."},"487":{"id":"/docs/concepts-29","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#jackie-os-agent-any-editor-hermes-optional","content":"Jackie OS is portable files — the vault, the skills, the rules. Any AI coding tool that opens the `~/Jackie-OS` folder (**Claude Code**, **Cursor**, **Codex**) auto-reads `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` and runs the skills that live inside it, *becoming* a Jackie OS agent; the skills aren't moved or copied — a few cross-project ones (e.g. `wrap up`) are installed once in `~/.agents/skills/`. `wrap up` from any editor syncs the vault, `## Status`, and `hot.md`, then commits. **Hermes** (below) is simply the always-on instance of that same agent on the VPS — it runs the schedule unattended. Hermes is not required to use the system; it only automates the loop."},"488":{"id":"/docs/concepts-30","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#okf-open-knowledge-format-bundle","content":"Jackie-OS adopts **Open Knowledge Format** *frontmatter* — every skill, solution, concept, project note, daily, and brief carries structured YAML (`type`, `title`, `timestamp`, …). This makes the vault a **portable, vendor-neutral knowledge bundle**: anyone can fork the structure and wire a different automation layer, and any agent can orient and retrieve by metadata instead of inferring from prose. **Frontmatter only** — internal links stay as Obsidian wikilinks (OKF's relative-link convention is *not* adopted). Backfilled by `System/tools/add-okf-frontmatter.py`; enforced by `janitor` OKF lint mode. Headline goal = portability; faster agent orientation/retrieval is the day-to-day payoff."},"489":{"id":"/docs/concepts-31","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"The VPS worker layer — runs the Hermes agent, crons, and the ops exec allowlist. **Models run on subscription OAuth CLIs, not API-price billing** (Nous Portal credits exhausted 2026-07-06; owner opted out of API pricing). Two Hermes profiles (as of 2026-07-10):"},"490":{"id":"/docs/concepts-32","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"Profile"},"491":{"id":"/docs/concepts-33","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"Model"},"492":{"id":"/docs/concepts-34","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"Auth"},"493":{"id":"/docs/concepts-35","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"Used for"},"494":{"id":"/docs/concepts-36","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"**`default`** (live gateway)"},"495":{"id":"/docs/concepts-37","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"`claude-fable-5` @ `high` effort → `claude-haiku-4.5` → `gpt-5.6-terra`"},"496":{"id":"/docs/concepts-38","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"Claude sub OAuth token; Codex CLI OAuth for Terra"},"497":{"id":"/docs/concepts-39","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"briefs, journal, cron ops, `@persik_hermes_bot`"},"498":{"id":"/docs/concepts-40","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"**`persiknewfin`**"},"499":{"id":"/docs/concepts-41","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"`gpt-5.6-terra` @ `xhigh` effort → `gpt-oss-120b:free` (OpenRouter) → `gemini-2.5-flash`"},"500":{"id":"/docs/concepts-42","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"Codex CLI OAuth; OpenRouter + Gemini API keys"},"501":{"id":"/docs/concepts-43","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"manual/gateway agentic runs (web + terminal toolsets, verify-on-stop)"},"502":{"id":"/docs/concepts-44","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"Auxiliary roles (vision, web-extract, compression, title generation, delegation subagents, …) run `gpt-5.4-mini` (Codex CLI OAuth) with `claude-haiku-4.5` fallback."},"503":{"id":"/docs/concepts-45","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps","content":"Newfin's `/ask` + `/research` shell the **subscription OAuth CLIs directly** (Claude Code / Codex), not a Hermes profile. Voice/photo STT stays direct-Gemini with Newfin's own key×model failover (`gemini-media-chain`, fallback `gemini-3.5-flash`). Source: newfin `plans/decisions-log.md` 2026-07-06 + 2026-07-04."},"504":{"id":"/docs/concepts-46","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#two-bot-model","content":"Two live Telegram bots, split by audience:"},"505":{"id":"/docs/concepts-47","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#two-bot-model","content":"**@Persik\\_finbot** — the Newfin-hosted Telegram product bot: money COO, `/day`, `/week`, spouse-scoped routes, **and owner ops** (`status`, `sync vault&#x60;). Credentials stay on Vercel; never deployed to the Hermes VPS. **`/ask` and `/research` run subscription OAuth CLIs directly** (Claude Code / Codex — not a Hermes profile, since 2026-07-06). `/research` routes through the Persik **counsel lane** as an agentic, web-searching research turn (`web` toolset) that relates findings to the owner's book only when they connect; `live_market` keeps a synchronous Binance price path. `/scout` + `/deep-research` were folded into `/research` (2026-06-30)."},"506":{"id":"/docs/concepts-48","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#two-bot-model","content":"**@persik\\_hermes\\_bot** — the **full** Telegram channel for the Hermes VPS agent: COO, CTO, journal, crons, ops — everything the Hermes agent does. Uses the Hermes model failover chain (see Hermes VPS). Reaches Newfin's `/v1` API for finance answers; does not ship to customers."},"507":{"id":"/docs/concepts-49","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps-1","content":"**Host:** `hermes@your-vps-host` — runs the `hermes` Linux user."},"508":{"id":"/docs/concepts-50","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-vps-1","content":"**What it is:** A full Claude Agent SDK instance — not just a cron host. Has a web dashboard (tunnel: `127.0.0.1:9119`) and a Headroom LLM proxy (`127.0.0.1:8787`)."},"509":{"id":"/docs/concepts-51","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"Layer"},"510":{"id":"/docs/concepts-52","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"Owner"},"511":{"id":"/docs/concepts-53","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"Jobs"},"512":{"id":"/docs/concepts-54","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"Hermes Agent cron (dashboard → Cron tab)"},"513":{"id":"/docs/concepts-55","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"Hermes SDK"},"514":{"id":"/docs/concepts-56","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"morning-brief, journal-capture, telegram-sweep, trade-digest"},"515":{"id":"/docs/concepts-57","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"OS crontab (`crontab -l`)"},"516":{"id":"/docs/concepts-58","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"`hermes` user"},"517":{"id":"/docs/concepts-59","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"autodeploy, merge-poll, healthcheck, degraded-brief, intel-weekly, cbm-index, janitor-skills-audit"},"518":{"id":"/docs/concepts-60","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"Mac weekly-review schedule (Cowork, otherwise retired)"},"519":{"id":"/docs/concepts-61","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"macOS"},"520":{"id":"/docs/concepts-62","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"weekly-review (Sun 18:00 — the only remaining Mac-scheduled task)"},"521":{"id":"/docs/concepts-63","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#three-cron-system-must-not-overlap","content":"Adding a job to multiple layers causes double-runs — always check all three before adding a scheduled task. &#x2A;(Research auto-run fully retired 2026-06-30; Persik `/research` is now agentic in Newfin.)*"},"522":{"id":"/docs/concepts-64","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"When"},"523":{"id":"/docs/concepts-65","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Trigger"},"524":{"id":"/docs/concepts-66","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"What syncs"},"525":{"id":"/docs/concepts-67","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Authoritative?"},"526":{"id":"/docs/concepts-68","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"**Daily 07:30 Warsaw**"},"527":{"id":"/docs/concepts-69","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Scheduled daily or \"morning brief\" / \"daily brief\""},"528":{"id":"/docs/concepts-70","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Project notes `## Status` (rolling 24h window), `hot.md` active lines, Ops board (if exists), brief `## Log`"},"529":{"id":"/docs/concepts-71","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Vault project notes (Status is source of truth)"},"530":{"id":"/docs/concepts-72","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"**:25 every 2h, VPS crontab**"},"531":{"id":"/docs/concepts-73","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Scheduled system crontab"},"532":{"id":"/docs/concepts-74","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"External code repos (via API), thin `## Status` prepend"},"533":{"id":"/docs/concepts-75","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"GitHub/git repos (merge-poll reads via API; not a rich sync)"},"534":{"id":"/docs/concepts-76","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"**Session-end + step 0 of morning-brief**"},"535":{"id":"/docs/concepts-77","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"`/wrap-up` command OR wrap-up OR \"sync projects\" OR after `~/dev` PR merge/push"},"536":{"id":"/docs/concepts-78","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Registry: git repos, `STATUS.md` files, vault notes, `hot.md`, ops-board lanes; Linear task state (if `tracker: linear`)"},"537":{"id":"/docs/concepts-79","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Each source type: git log, status-file hash, vault note, Linear API — code wins"},"538":{"id":"/docs/concepts-80","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"**End of working session**"},"539":{"id":"/docs/concepts-81","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"`/wrap-up` / `/wrap-up all` / `/wrap-up merge` OR wrap-up OR after code-repo merge/push"},"540":{"id":"/docs/concepts-82","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Status prepend (shipped/next/blocked), brief `## Log`, `hot.md` full overwrite, plans/catalog"},"541":{"id":"/docs/concepts-83","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Latest work in session (code repo or changed vault notes); plans only if realized"},"542":{"id":"/docs/concepts-84","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#single-llm-gateway-hermes-cli","content":"All AI calls from Newfin bot, Jackie-OS skills, and Hermes agent tasks route through **one gateway: the `hermes` CLI** on the VPS. This is the Claude Agent SDK CLI. There is no direct OpenAI/Anthropic call from Newfin's backend — it goes through Hermes."},"543":{"id":"/docs/concepts-85","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#single-llm-gateway-hermes-cli","content":"**Exception:** speech-to-text (Newfin voice features) calls the STT provider directly, not via Hermes CLI."},"544":{"id":"/docs/concepts-86","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#linear-integration--autonomous-agents","content":"**Project tracking:** B-Unit is the first product tracked in **Linear** (workspace `evegelin`, project `B-Unit&#x60;). Task state syncs on ship per the contract, and reads back into project-sync/morning-brief via the registry &#x2A;*`tracker: linear`** flag; all other projects stay `tracker: bases`, markdown-only (`roadmap-index.md` + `future-improvements.md`) until Linear rolls out. New repos onboard via `linear-project-rollout` skill."},"545":{"id":"/docs/concepts-87","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#linear-integration--autonomous-agents","content":"**Autonomous agents:** Four Cyrus-instance agents on the Hermes VPS dispatch from Linear → isolated worktree → tested PR with `Fixes &#60;ISSUE-ID>` → In Review → human merges (agents never merge or push default branches). **Fablio** (Claude Fable 5 — CEO/CPO/CTO orchestrator; `Plan`/`Scope` PM modes), **Cursorio** (Cursor — fast implementer; `Build`/`Bug` modes), **Codexio** (Codex GPT-5.6 Sol — design lead), **Cyrusio** (Claude Sonnet 5 — delivery engineer). Hermes stays the general-purpose VPS agent (not a Linear worker). Legacy ChatGPT Codex in CI still exists. Route by repo label + optional mode label + assignee/delegate."},"546":{"id":"/docs/concepts-88","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#how-newfin-uses-hermes","content":"Newfin backend → SSH → `hermes-ops-exec.sh` (named Hermes operation) → `hermes` CLI → Anthropic API."},"547":{"id":"/docs/concepts-89","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#how-newfin-uses-hermes","content":"`@persik_hermes_bot` is the direct channel to the Hermes VPS agent for all work (COO, CTO, ops). What's retired is the old relay: `@Persik_finbot` proxying `/work` commands over SSH to Hermes — that path no longer exists."},"548":{"id":"/docs/concepts-90","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#what-lives-where-post-2026-06-29-restructure","content":"Path"},"549":{"id":"/docs/concepts-91","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#what-lives-where-post-2026-06-29-restructure","content":"Contents"},"550":{"id":"/docs/concepts-92","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#what-lives-where-post-2026-06-29-restructure","content":"`~/jackie-os/`"},"551":{"id":"/docs/concepts-93","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#what-lives-where-post-2026-06-29-restructure","content":"Jackie-OS repo — vault, skills, plans (git-synced every 2 min via autodeploy)"},"552":{"id":"/docs/concepts-94","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#what-lives-where-post-2026-06-29-