lem-this-solves","content":"The problem this solves"},"1579":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-3","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"The second brain (vault)"},"1580":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-4","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"What it actually does"},"1581":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-5","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"The agent (Hermes)"},"1582":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-6","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional--it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"Hermes is optional — it lives in a folder"},"1583":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-7","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-they-connect","content":"How they connect"},"1584":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-8","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"How a day actually feels"},"1585":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-9","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"What the agent is allowed to touch"},"1586":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-10","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"The commands (everything else is automatic)"},"1587":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-11","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"The tools, in plain words"},"1588":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-12","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-core-idea-in-one-line","content":"The core idea in one line"},"1589":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-13","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-is","content":"A **second brain** plus an **always-on AI agent** — wired together so the agent actually knows what's in the brain."},"1590":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-14","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-is","content":"The second brain is your Obsidian vault: every journal entry, project note, decision, and idea, linked and versioned in git. It compounds over time. The agent (Hermes) lives on a server in Germany, runs 24/7, reads the vault before doing anything, and delivers results back to Telegram."},"1591":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-15","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-is","content":"Together: you think and decide, the brain remembers, the agent acts."},"1592":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-16","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Every time you open ChatGPT or Claude, it starts with zero context. You re-explain your projects, your priorities, what you shipped last week. The AI is helpful in a session but amnesiac across them."},"1593":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-17","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Most people also have this split:"},"1594":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-18","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Notes (diary, ideas, plans) — in one app"},"1595":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-19","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Code projects — in separate folders"},"1596":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-20","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"AI — in a chat window that forgot everything"},"1597":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-21","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Nothing shares memory. Jackie OS makes all three read from the same source."},"1598":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-22","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"The vault is a folder of markdown files you open in Obsidian. Notes link to each other like Wikipedia — `[[Newfin]]`, `[[Warsaw]]`, `[[2026-06-20]]`. Over time you get a web: journal connects to projects, projects connect to decisions, decisions connect to people."},"1599":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-23","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"What lives there:"},"1600":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-24","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Written by you"},"1601":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-25","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Written by the agent"},"1602":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-26","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Daily journal"},"1603":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-27","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Morning brief + weekly / monthly / yearly reviews"},"1604":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-28","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Project ideas, decisions"},"1605":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-29","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Project `## Status` (synced from code)"},"1606":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-30","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Notes on people, places"},"1607":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-31","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Clippings (links you sent) + person profiles"},"1608":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-32","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Beliefs, theses"},"1609":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-33","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Coaching notes, link suggestions, `hot.md` cache"},"1610":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-34","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"**hot.md** is the key mechanism: after every sync, the agent writes a fresh \\~500-word summary of what's currently active. Every AI session (Cursor, Claude Code, Hermes) reads this first. That's why context is never lost — there's a standing summary of where you are."},"1611":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-35","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"The vault is git-versioned. Nothing gets lost. The agent never edits your journal entries — only appends to the end, or writes into its own files."},"1612":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-36","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Every file also carries a little structured metadata (`type`, `title`, `date`) in a format called **OKF** (Open Knowledge Format). You never see it, but it makes the vault *portable* — not locked to any one tool — and lets any agent orient and retrieve by metadata instead of guessing from prose."},"1613":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-37","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"The system isn't one feature — it's a set of jobs the agent does for you, all reading from and writing to the same second brain."},"1614":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-38","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Vaulting & linking** — keeping one git-versioned source of truth *and* weaving it into a graph. Every note, brief, and decision lives in the vault; nothing is scattered or lost. After each brief, the agent also suggests links between notes you wrote — \"this journal entry relates to \\[\\[Newfin]], to \\[\\[Warsaw]]\" — so over time the vault becomes a connected web, not a pile of files."},"1615":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-39","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Capturing** — pulling stuff *into* the brain without friction. DM the Telegram bot a thought → it lands in today's journal within the hour. Send a link → it gets filed into Clippings. Type `meet Sarah:` with notes → it creates a meeting entry *and* a person note for Sarah."},"1616":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-40","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Briefing** — telling you where you are. Morning brief (daily), weekly review (Sunday), monthly and yearly reviews. Each reads the vault + your code and summarizes what changed, what's next, what's blocked."},"1617":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-41","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Syncing** — keeping code and notes in agreement. The agent reads git history from your repos and writes it into each project's `## Status` note, so the vault always reflects what actually shipped."},"1618":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-42","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Building** — it doesn't just *track* your code, it writes it. Acting as your CTO (through Claude Code), the agent implements features, fixes bugs, and ships — then syncs the result back into the vault. It's COO and CTO at once."},"1619":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-43","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Researching** — digging on demand. Say `research &lt;topic>` and it sweeps Reddit, HN, X, markets (last 30 days) and files the findings into the vault."},"1620":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-44","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Coaching** — the reflective layer. Recovery, identity, and \"fractal\" period reviews — week, month, year — where the agent takes a coach stance and walks you through patterns instead of just reporting facts."},"1621":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-45","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Enriching** — filling in context. New person shows up in your notes? The agent pulls a public profile and adds a `## Public profile` section to their note."},"1622":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-46","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"Each of these is a **skill** — a markdown playbook the agent follows. They all share the same vault, so capturing feeds briefing, briefing feeds coaching, and nothing has to be re-explained between them."},"1623":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-47","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"The jobs above are *what* it does. Hermes is *who* does them — a Claude-powered agent, not a chatbot you open. It runs 24/7 on a server, works on a schedule while you sleep, and you can reach it any time by DMing `@persik_hermes_bot` on Telegram. It wears two hats: **COO** (briefs, sync, research, journal) and **CTO** (writes code, builds features, ships)."},"1624":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-48","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"Three things make it an agent rather than a script:"},"1625":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-49","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"**It runs itself.** A schedule on the server fires the jobs — morning brief at 07:30, journal capture hourly, weekly review Sunday. Your Mac can be off and traveling; the loop still runs."},"1626":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-50","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"**It follows playbooks, not hardcode.** Each job is a **skill** — a markdown file in `System/skills/` that lives *in the vault*. You read and edit them like any other note. Change the playbook, change the behavior."},"1627":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-51","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"**It's not a black box.** Everything it reads comes from the vault; everything it writes goes back to the vault. The full chain is auditable — no hidden state."},"1628":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-52","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"There's a second, separate bot — `@Persik_finbot` — that handles money and finance for the Newfin app. Hermes (`@persik_hermes_bot`) is the one that runs your OS."},"1629":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-53","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional--it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"Hermes is the *always-on* layer: it runs the schedule on a server while you sleep. But you don't need it to use Jackie OS."},"1630":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-54","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional--it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"At its core, Jackie OS is just a folder of files — your notes, the skills, the rules. Open that folder in **Claude Code**, **Cursor**, or **Codex** and that tool *becomes* a Jackie OS agent. It auto-reads the same `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md` rules the moment the folder is open, and the skills are right there inside it. (A few cross-project skills like **wrap up** are installed once on your Mac, so they work in every project.)"},"1631":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-55","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional--it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"Nothing \"migrates\" — you just connect the folder. Say **wrap up** from any of these tools and the vault syncs, project `## Status` blocks update, `hot.md` refreshes, and the changes commit — exactly the loop Hermes runs, just triggered by hand."},"1632":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-56","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional--it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"So: **Hermes = the schedule** (automation while you sleep). &#x2A;*Your IDE + the folder = the same system, on demand.** Same brain either way."},"1633":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-57","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-they-connect","content":"It's a loop, not a pipeline. You feed the vault (journaling, DMs, code). Hermes reads the vault + git, does its jobs, writes back to the vault, and pings you on Telegram. Your DMs flow back into the vault. Round and round."},"1634":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-58","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-they-connect","content":"The glue is **hot.md**. When *any* Claude session starts — terminal, Cursor, Hermes — it reads hot.md first and walks in knowing your current focus, last merge, what's pending. That's the trick that kills the cold start."},"1635":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-59","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-they-connect","content":"For the system diagram, see the docs site \"The system map\" page."},"1636":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-60","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**07:30*&#x2A; — Hermes wakes up (you're asleep), reads all your code repos, sees what merged, syncs project status notes, writes the brief, sends it to your Telegram. Done before you check your phone. &#x2A;(Research is on-demand now — say `research &lt;topic>` whenever you want it; it no longer runs unattended at 06:45.)*"},"1637":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-61","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**Morning** — You read the brief over coffee. Reply to Hermes via Telegram DM if you want to add something to your journal. It captures it within the hour."},"1638":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-62","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**Day** — You work, code, journal in Obsidian. When you finish a planning session or push code, say **wrap up** — Hermes syncs the vault immediately."},"1639":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-63","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**Sunday 18:00** — Weekly review runs automatically. Patterns, what compounded, what to carry forward."},"1640":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-64","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**Nothing requires you.** The morning stack runs on the VPS even when your Mac is off and you're traveling."},"1641":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-65","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"**Yes:**"},"1642":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-66","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Write briefs and reviews into `Vault/Briefs/`"},"1643":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-67","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Update `## Status` blocks in project notes"},"1644":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-68","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Append to today's journal (Telegram capture only — end of file)"},"1645":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-69","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Refresh `hot.md` after every sync"},"1646":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-70","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"**Never:**"},"1647":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-71","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Edit the body of your journal entries"},"1648":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-72","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Touch notes tagged `private`"},"1649":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-73","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Rename vault notes (that breaks Obsidian links — human-only)"},"1650":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-74","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Put credentials in any markdown file"},"1651":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-75","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","cont